# Wave W17-Q (Route 123): master elm — a tended field elm in rich greens, broad and kept, its crown trimmed by years of the berry hands’ ladders, highlight lifted clear of the turf, on master turf (ground baked in). Route 123’s own tree — richer and more kept than Route 117’s open field elm: this elm works for a living, and its crown shows the care.
